m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Histidine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: The network leverages prebiotic carboxylic acid and amino acid chemistry for C3 and C4 pool buildup, assembling the imidazole ring from plausibly prebiotic imidazole or precursor synthesis routes, then conjugating to an alpha-amino acid backbone. It incorporates C1 chemistry (formaldehyde/formamide), glycolaldehyde, Strecker-type amino acid formation, plausible imidazole-forming routes (amidines, cyanamides, diamines), as well as direct condensation and cyclization. Hydrothermal, surface, and prebiotic pool environments are used as justified, with mineral and UV catalysis where appropriate. All reactions are explicitly atom- and charge-balanced, with each transformation justified from the literature or by established prebiotic plausibility.\n\nMOLECULES (16 nodes):\n  - mol_001: CO (carbon monoxide) [starting]\n  - mol_002: H2 (hydrogen gas) [starting]\n  - mol_003: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_004: CH2O (formaldehyde) [intermediate]\n  - mol_005: HOCH2CHO (glycolaldehyde) [intermediate]\n  - mol_006: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_007: C2H5NO2 (glycine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C3H7NO2 (alanine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C3H3N3 (imidazole-4-carbonitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C3H4N2 (imidazole) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_011: C3H6N2O2 (histidine minus carboxyl) [intermediate]\n  - mol_012: CH3CN (acetonitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_013: C2H3N (acetonitrile radical) [intermediate]\n  - mol_014: CH4N2 (diamino methane) [intermediate]\n  - mol_015: H2NCONH2 (urea) [intermediate]\n  - mol_016: C6H9N3O2 (Histidine) [target]\n\nREACTIONS (12 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_001, mol_002 -> mol_004 (CO reduction to formaldehyde) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_002: mol_004 -> mol_005 (Formose reaction to glycolaldehyde (C2)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_003: mol_004, mol_003, mol_006 -> mol_007 (Strecker synthesis of glycine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_004: mol_005, mol_003, mol_006 -> mol_008 (Strecker synthesis of alanine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_005: mol_003, mol_006 -> mol_010 (Imidazole ring formation from formamide) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_012, mol_006, mol_004 -> mol_007, mol_008 (Ammonolysis and hydrolysis of acetonitrile to glycine/alanine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_007: mol_010, mol_003 -> mol_009 (Alkylation of imidazole to imidazole-4-carbonitrile) [Surface]\n  - rxn_008: mol_009, mol_006 -> mol_010, mol_015 (Hydrolysis of imidazole-4-carbonitrile to imidazole and urea) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_009: mol_010, mol_008, mol_006 -> mol_016 (Histidine backbone build-up via condensation of imidazole and amino acid) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_010: mol_005, mol_006 -> mol_014 (Amination of glycolaldehyde to aminoacetaldehyde) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_011: mol_014, mol_003 -> mol_010 (Cyclization of aminoacetaldehyde with formamidine to give imidazole) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_012: mol_005, mol_015, mol_003 -> mol_010 (Addition of urea and glycolaldehyde for alternative imidazole synthesis) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Classical C1 \u2192 C2 \u2192 imidazole \u2192 histidine (5 steps)\n  - P2: Imidazole from HCN and ammonia, then histidine build-up (3 steps)\n  - P3: Hydrothermal diamino path to imidazole (4 steps)\n  - P4: Alternative nitrile pathway (5 steps)\n  - P5: Urea-glycolalde