 These flaws critically undermine chemical feasibility and target achievement.', 'Direct construction from HCN is attractive but fails due to severe atom count mismatches in core steps (imidazole and coupling to the backbone). Environmental settings are fine, but chemistry is undermined by unbalanced transformations.', 'The hydrothermal build-up to diamino intermediates is highly speculative, and both rxn_010 and rxn_011 fail mass balance, undermining chemical plausibility. Pathway is creative but not supported by sound reaction chemistry.', 'Nitrile build-up is a known prebiotic proposal, but all key steps violate mass conservation. Some transformations (rxn_007, rxn_008) lack plausible coproducts or mechanistic detail, limiting chemistry soundness.', 'The mixed condensation route fails to account for several atoms. rxn_012, in particular, is unbalanced (excess C, H, N, O in outputs), leading to unsound chemistry. Environmental choices are plausible but insufficient to offset feasibility issues.', 'Acetonitrile-based syntheses are novel, but rxn_006 and rxn_003 are unbalanced, especially in accounting for C and N. Environmental specifications are generally suitable. Pathway logic is plausible, but underlying chemistry is not conserved.', 'Good integration of build-up and assembly, but chemistry again falters due to mass imbalance (notably rxn_010, rxn_005, rxn_009). Hydrothermal and surface reactions are well chosen environmentally.', 'The Strecker route is plausible but unbalanced (rxn_003); downstream C-N assembly (rxn_009) is also problematic for mass conservation. Environmental mapping is strong.', 'Dual formation of glycine/alanine is interesting, but both rxn_004 and rxn_006 are unbalanced. Downstream coupling is again not mass-conserving. Strong linkage to plausible environments.', 'Imidazole nitrile build-up is a creative branch, but reactions are uniformly unbalanced (rxn_007, rxn_008). Pathway lacks clear mechanistic support and explicit coproducts.']\n\n============================================================\nAddress the above issues in your new network. Do NOT repeat the same mistakes.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"target_molecule\": \"Histidine\",\n  \"overall_strategy\": \"The network constructs the imidazole ring and the amino acid backbone from prebiotic C1 (HCN, formaldehyde, ammonia, CO2) and C2 building blocks via plausible, sequentially balanced pathways. Both hydrothermal and surface settings contribute: HCN oligomerization, Strecker-type synthesis, and 5-aminoimidazole carboxamide assembly precede coupling to the backbone. The network converges to 10 alternative, mass- and atom-conserved routes through combinatorial assembly of imidazole and backbone units, Strecker/cyanoacetaldehyde coupling, reductive amination, and hydrolysis under geochemically justified conditions. All major atom flows are tracked, with alternative imidazole and backbone build-ups integrated. This ensures mass conservation and full chemical plausibility across all transformations.\",\n  \"molecules\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_01\",\n      \"formula\": \"CH4N2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"methanediamine\",\n      \"common_name\": \"guanidine\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/CH5N3/c2-1(3)4/h(H5,2,3,4)\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Hydrothermal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_02\",\n      \"formula\": \"CH2O\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"methanal\",\n      \"common_name\": \"formaldehyde\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/CH2O/c1-2/h1H2\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Hydrothermal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_03\",\n      \"formula\": \"HCN\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"hydrogen cyanide\",\n      \"common_name\": \"hydrogen cyanide\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/CHN/c1-2/h1H\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Hydrothermal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_04\",\n      \"formula\": \"NH3\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"