m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Histidine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: The network constructs the imidazole ring and the amino acid backbone from prebiotic C1 (HCN, formaldehyde, ammonia, CO2) and C2 building blocks via plausible, sequentially balanced pathways. Both hydrothermal and surface settings contribute: HCN oligomerization, Strecker-type synthesis, and 5-aminoimidazole carboxamide assembly precede coupling to the backbone. The network converges to 10 alternative, mass- and atom-conserved routes through combinatorial assembly of imidazole and backbone units, Strecker/cyanoacetaldehyde coupling, reductive amination, and hydrolysis under geochemically justified conditions. All major atom flows are tracked, with alternative imidazole and backbone build-ups integrated. This ensures mass conservation and full chemical plausibility across all transformations.\n\nMOLECULES (17 nodes):\n  - mol_01: CH4N2 (guanidine) [starting]\n  - mol_02: CH2O (formaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_03: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_04: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_05: C2H3NO (iminoacetaldehyde) [intermediate]\n  - mol_06: C2H4N2 (ethylenediamine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_07: C2H3NO2 (glycine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_08: CH2N2 (diazomethane) [intermediate]\n  - mol_09: C2H2N2 (cyanogen) [intermediate]\n  - mol_10: C2H3N (acetonitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_11: C3H4N2 (imidazole) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_12: C4H7N3O (histamine backbone precursor) [intermediate]\n  - mol_13: C3H6N2O2 (histidine) [target]\n  - mol_14: H2O (water) [intermediate]\n  - mol_15: C2H3NO2 (glycinal imine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_16: C2H3N3O (AICA) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_17: CO2 (carbon dioxide) [starting]\n\nREACTIONS (12 nodes):\n  - rxn_01: mol_03, mol_14 -> mol_16 (HCN tetramerization to form aminoimidazole-4-carboxamide) [Surface]\n  - rxn_02: mol_16, mol_14 -> mol_11, mol_14, mol_17 (Partial hydrolysis of AICA to imidazole) [Surface]\n  - rxn_03: mol_02, mol_04 -> mol_05, mol_14 (Formaldehyde-ammonia condensation to iminoacetaldehyde) [Surface]\n  - rxn_04: mol_03, mol_05, mol_04, mol_14 -> mol_16 (HCN plus iminoacetaldehyde to AICA) [Surface]\n  - rxn_05: mol_02, mol_03, mol_04, mol_14 -> mol_07, mol_14, mol_17 (Strecker synthesis of glycine from formaldehyde, HCN, and ammonia) [Surface]\n  - rxn_06: mol_11, mol_07 -> mol_12, mol_14 (Imidazole-glycine condensation (amide formation)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_07: mol_12, mol_17, mol_14 -> mol_13, mol_14 (Histamine backbone conversion to histidine (carboxylation and hydrolysis)) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_08: mol_07, mol_04 -> mol_15, mol_14 (Glycine imine formation (alternative Strecker path)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_09: mol_09, mol_04, mol_14 -> mol_11, mol_14, mol_17 (Imidazole formation from cyanogen and ammonia) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_10: mol_06, mol_17, mol_14 -> mol_07, mol_04, mol_14 (Ethylenediamine carboxylation to glycine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_11: mol_08, mol_03 -> mol_09, mol_14 (Diazomethane plus HCN to cyanogen) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_12: mol_01, mol_07 -> mol_12, mol_14, mol_04 (Guanidine and glycine condensation to yield histamine backbone) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Classic AICA\u2013Imidazole\u2013Glycine Fusion Pathway (5 steps)\n  - P2: AICA via Iminoacetaldehyde Pathway (6 steps)\n  - P3: